0002-msvc-branch-relocation-fields

Branch relocations (REL24/REL14) in Microsoft PowerPC COFF: the linker adds the distance from the
start of the instruction's section to the target, so the field holds minus the instruction's offset
within its section. A zero field lands every cross-object call its own offset too far.

diff --git a/src/util/xex.rs b/src/util/xex.rs
index 722b92e..b8f8454 100644
--- a/src/util/xex.rs
+++ b/src/util/xex.rs
@@ -480,10 +480,16 @@ fn adjusted_data_for_relocs(section: &ObjSection) -> Result<Vec<u8>> {
                 ins &= !0xFFFF;
             }
             ObjRelocKind::PpcRel24 => {
-                ins &= !0x3FFFFFC;
+                // Microsoft's convention for PowerPC branch relocations: the field holds minus the instruction's
+                // offset within its section, and the linker adds the target's offset from the section start.
+                // A zero field makes every branch land its own section offset too far.
+                let field = (addr as i32).wrapping_neg() as u32 & 0x3FFFFFC;
+                ins = (ins & !0x3FFFFFC) | field;
             }
             ObjRelocKind::PpcRel14 => {
-                ins &= !0xFFFC;
+                // Same convention; the 16-bit field only fits when the offset is below 32 KB.
+                let field = (addr as i32).wrapping_neg() as u32 & 0xFFFC;
+                ins = (ins & !0xFFFC) | field;
             }
